eed via a longer, self-sufficient route that does not rely on you.\n\nLet me know if you can cover those Reds—otherwise, I will not be cooperating. \n, \nplayer 0: Thank you for your clear summary. I can indeed cover your Red chip costs at the following tiles:\n\n- (1, 0): I give you an R\n- (2, 1): I give you an R\n\nIn exchange, you cover my Blue chip costs at:\n\n- (0, 2): You give me a B\n- (1, 3): You give me a B\n\n**Restating the full contract for clarity:**\n\n- (0, 2): You give me a B\n- (1, 3): You give me a B\n- (1, 0): I give you an R\n- (2, 1): I give you an R\n\nLet’s proceed with this contract if you agree. Please confirm. \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: I confirm the terms as stated:\n\n- (0, 2): I give you a B  \n- (1, 3): I give you a B  \n- (1, 0): You give me an R  \n- (2, 1): You give me an R  \n\nThis contract allows both of us to strictly benefit and reach our respective goals with the highest score possible.\n\n**agree** \n, \nplayer 0: **agree** \n",
